WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.501
-That's a movie star!

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.400
That's a stud right there.
Welcome.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.701
It is great to see you.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.434
Thank you for being here
in person. I appreciate that.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.234
-Well, it's very nice to be here
in person. Thank you.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.000
-How are the family?
How are the kids?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.801
-They're good.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:16.667
-Their thing at the moment
is just screaming.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.667
-Ah, that sounds peaceful.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:19.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.734
-They're, like, really good
at it, you know.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.200
But it's all -- you know, like,
our 8-year-old,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.801
I feel like she is going through
some kind of --

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.000
Apparently, we've since found
out that around eight,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.234
they get some hormonal surge.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:35.033
And she's just, like, guttural
screaming a lot,

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.400
which encourages the 2-year-old,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.133
who is doing that anyway
in her own kind of way.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.133
And then the 5-year-old sits
in the middle just like going,

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.200
"I may as well join in."
-Yeah.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.734
And you're just driving going,
"This is awesome."

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.701
-But occasionally, we take
a break to listen to

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.601
the soundtrack for "Encanto."

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:50.934
That's our -- Yeah.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.467
-I mean, that's what everyone's
doing right now.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.000
-That's what everyone's doing.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.100
-That represents everyone.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.033
It's screaming and "Encanto"
right now.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:59.200
-How good is the music?
-We don't talk about Bruno.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Yeah, I mean, come on.
-We might talk about Bruno.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.667
-Exactly. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.400
-We're allowed to talk about
Bruno.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.801
-Speaking of singing,
by the way,

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.968
I saw a really cool thing.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.534
You were singing
"Rainbow Connection."

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:12.167
-I was.
-In the Kermit the Frog voice.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.467
I have it here.
Can we just show it?

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:20.000
-♪ Why are there so many songs
about rainbows? ♪

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.634
♪ What's on the other side? ♪

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:29.801
-Nailed it! Nailed it!

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.334
-Yeah.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:34.767
-It looks like you might be
singing to your girls there.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:37.000
-I'm not. That's sad, I'm not.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.267
-You're not?
-I'm just singing to my groomer

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.033
before I go on
another talk show.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.033
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.567
-There were no kids in the room?
-No.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.100
I'm not even sure my kids have
seen that.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:51.901
I was mucking around with a
guitar and I was just --

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:55.367
I've always loved that song, you
know, so I was singing that song

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:59.567
anyway and then realized that
I could sing it like Kermit.

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.667
-I love that you could do
something like that

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.133
but then you could also do
"Belfast."

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.434
I mean, you're kind of
doing everything.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.601
-That's the idea, isn't it?

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.534
-Yeah, I guess that's the fun of
acting, yeah.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.534
Congrats.
It's getting great reviews.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:13.868
It's been nominated for
every award I can think of.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.234
You're getting Oscar buzz.
That must be exciting.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.467
I mean, I know it's --
You're going around

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.501
and you're on all of the lists
and everything like that,

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:24.300
but for anyone who hasn't seen
"Belfast," can you set it up?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.367
What it's about?
-Yeah.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.467
Yeah, so it's --
our writer/director

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:29.767
Sir Kenneth Branagh --
-Kenneth Branagh. Awesome.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.601
-Who's just a legend.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.234
-It's sort of
semi-autobiographical

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.601
about his childhood growing up
in Belfast.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:37.734
A lot of people don't realize he
has any connection to Ireland.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:41.267
But he was brought up
in Belfast.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:44.868
We go from 1969
when he was nine years old

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.701
and follow the beginning of
the conflict,

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:50.400
which would go on for 30 years,
we know, and its troubles,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.868
and it's a sort of 9-year-old
boy's account of his family

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.167
and how they were dealing with
that situation at that time.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.801
-Now, were born and raised
in Belfast?

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.801
-Yep.
-And I read that you were

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:03.934
the only actor that Kenneth
considered for the role.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.901
That's got to feel good.
-He's lost his mind.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.834
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:11.300
I mean, that's -- Have you ever
met Kenneth Branagh before

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.701
or come close to working
with him?

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.367
-I did audition for "Thor"

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.701
when he directed "Thor"
way back when.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.968
But I didn't -- you know, I'd --
I've talked to Ken about --

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.634
I don't even think he saw
my tape, it was that bad.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.167
-To play Thor?
-No, no -- like, no.

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.501
I don't know, one of the guys.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:29.701
-One of his buddies.
-Yeah, one of his, you know --

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.701
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Smaller buddies, I think.

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:37.934
But Ken -- I grew up with
a picture of Kenneth Branagh

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:41.000
on our bookshelf
of him and my dad.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.968
My dad was a professor of
medicine,

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:46.501
and he opened a maternity ward
at the hospital

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.667
my dad spent the majority
of his career at.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.868
So there's a picture of my dad
with Kenneth Branagh

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:53.033
and a couple of other doctors
always in my house.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.334
-Really?
-Yeah, it was cool.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:57.200
Sort of full circle.
-I loved it.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.701
Obviously, I'm Irish -- Fallon.
-Yep.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:04.934
-But I loved it because it was
a different type of Irish movie

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.400
that you would see out there
and, like --

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.100
you kind of go like -- I loved
it, I appreciated it.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.801
But it's really just a family is
what it was really about.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:15.634
-Yeah, and I think that's why
it's resonated so well.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.868
You know, we're making a movie
about a tiny place

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.667
on a tiny island that people
don't really know

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.767
that much about really,
even though we've spread

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.534
ourselves pretty far, the Irish.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:26.534
But, you know, we -- it is at
a particular point in time,

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.434
but it is essentially,
as you said,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.934
it's about a family and it's
about family dealing with crisis

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:35.300
and we can all -- every single
person here can understand that.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.033
-Yeah. Does it -- There's a part
of the movie towards the middle,

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:42.167
towards the end, but you end up
just singing --

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.200
♪ Everlasting love ♪

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.334
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:51.334
It's such a great song,
But it's at the perfect part of

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.801
the movie because it's been
such a tough thing to watch.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:58.133
And that scene to me was
my scene because

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:01.200
I loved it because I saw you
guys were just in love.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.067
-Yeah, listen,
it's been a lovely --

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.067
The response to that scene
has been incredible.

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:09.634
And for us, it's a moment of
escapism and a release that you

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.033
kind of need at that point
in the film.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:14.634
But also, like, it's essentially
about through the medium of song

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:18.000
these two central characters, my
character saying to his wife,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.901
"Look, we are going through
the wringer here.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:22.534
This is tough but I've got you.

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:23.968
Don't worry. I've got you.
I love you.

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:26.667
It's going to be okay
and that's not changing."

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.267
-That's what I'm talking
about it, yeah.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:31.033
Is it nerve-wracking to just
sing and just dance and --

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.734
-Yeah, I've been doing it
too much recently.

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:34.767
-Kermit the Frog, yeah.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:38.334
-I mean, that's a choice,
a bad choice, but, you know.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.000
The last few things
I've ended up singing.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.467
But I think I know what
I'm doing next

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.701
and I know I don't sing in it so
we are all going to be spared.

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:44.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.167
I want to talk more
about the movie

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.501
and show a clip
when we come back.

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.467
More with Jamie Dornan
after the break. Come on back.

